1. Definitions
   "Licensor" means itge.e. "Purchaser" means the natural person who bought a
   licence to the Software from the Licensor (for example through the Inai
   website) or who received a written licence from the Licensor. "Your Devices"
   means computers and other devices owned or controlled by the Purchaser for
   the Purchaser's own use.

2. Licence grant
   Subject to this licence and to payment of the applicable fee, the Licensor
   grants the Purchaser a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
   non-sublicensable licence to:
   (a) install and use the Software on Your Devices, for the Purchaser's own
       personal and business purposes; and
   (b) modify the Software and create derivative works for that same own use.
   One licence covers one person. Teams, companies and classes need one licence
   per person or a separate written agreement with the Licensor.

3. Restrictions
   The Purchaser may NOT, without the Licensor's prior written permission:
   (a) redistribute, publish, share, upload or otherwise make the Software (or
       any modified version or substantial part of it) available to anyone else,
       including in a public or shared repository, marketplace or course;
   (b) sublicense, sell, resell, rent, lend or transfer the Software or this
       licence;
   (c) use the Software to build or offer a competing product, template or
       service that substitutes for the Software;
   (d) remove or alter copyright notices, this licence or the third-party notices.
   The Purchaser's own notes, vault content and data created with the Software
   belong to the Purchaser and are not covered by these restrictions.

4. Contributions
   If the Purchaser (or any participant of a Founder Matrix programme, such as
   SB+AI Season 2 students) submits a contribution to the Licensor — for example
   a pull request, patch, issue text, skill, script or documentation — the
   contributor:
   (a) assigns to the Licensor all copyright and other rights in the
       contribution, or, where an assignment is not permitted by law, grants the
       Licensor a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free, exclusive,
       transferable and sublicensable licence to use, modify, distribute and sell
       it as part of the Software or otherwise;
   (b) confirms that the contribution is their own original work (or that they
       have the right to submit it) and that it does not include anyone else's
       personal or confidential data; and
   (c) waives, to the extent permitted by law, any moral rights that would
       restrict the Licensor's use of the contribution.
   Contributions are voluntary and unpaid unless agreed otherwise in writing.

5. Third-party components
   The Software does not bundle third-party code. Official plugins and tools that
   the setup offers to install (see plugins/fm/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) are
   installed from their own sources and remain under their own licences and
   terms; this licence does not apply to them.

6. Termination
   This licence ends automatically if the Purchaser breaches it. On termination
   the Purchaser must stop using and delete all copies of the Software (the
   Purchaser keeps their own notes and data).

7. No warranty
   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
